      "message": "\u003e the add function only accepts int, so I cannot use dt_nodelabel_reg_size_hex, but rather dt_nodelabel_reg_size_int.\n\nSorry that I didn\u0027t notice that the add function supports only `int` type. Thanks for the correction.\n\n\u003eSo this default value will be without the if statement if $(dt_nodelabel_exists,sram0\nif this is the case, do we need the other defaults per product?\n\nI think all of the npcx devices should have to define the DT nodes `sram0`.\nMaybe you can remove `if $(dt_nodelabel_exists,sram0`\n\nAs this change directly calculate the size from DT nodes, the following per product defaults can also be remove:\n```\ndefault 0x00018000 if SOC_NPCX9MFP\ndefault 0x00020000 if SOC_NPCX9M7FB\ndefault 0x00010000\n```\n\nBy the way, I just notice that it seems the config `CROS_EC_DATA_RAM_SIZE` is no longer used in the EC repo by searching all the EC source folder.",
